{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds","id":1072653,"title":"Freeholds","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-04-03T12:22:52-07:00","id":1072653,"title":"Freeholds","content":"I've had some Changeling books sitting on my shelves for a few years but only really read the core book. I'm toying with the idea of a Changeling game, so I was looking to create a fictional city. Something I'm not totally clear on, is what the courts do on a day to day basis. I'm more familiar with kindred society and can see how their political system would work, governing feeding rights, enforcing the Masquerade and the other rules of the city. How a freehold functions isn't so obvious to me, so I'd would be interested to hear others' opinions on the political situation in a freehold.<br /> <br /> Assuming I go with the four season based courts, what would actually change when, for example, Summer gave way to Autumn?<br /> <br /> Does the court that is currently in power get to issue rules to the freehold or enforce/encourage seasonal traditions?<br /> Apart from the festivities associated with each court, would your 'average' changeling would they notice the change?<br /> <br /> I'm just about to start Lords of Summer, so it could be that the answers are in there, but I'd still be interested to hear how others have played it. Or if more details are in a different book?<br /> <br /> Cheers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3955-roguewind","name":"Roguewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T13:02:13-07:00","id":1072671,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Roguewind</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds#post1072653\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've had some Changeling books sitting on my shelves for a few years but only really read the core book. I'm toying with the idea of a Changeling game, so I was looking to create a fictional city. Something I'm not totally clear on, is what the courts do on a day to day basis. I'm more familiar with kindred society and can see how their political system would work, governing feeding rights, enforcing the Masquerade and the other rules of the city. How a freehold functions isn't so obvious to me, so I'd would be interested to hear others' opinions on the political situation in a freehold.</div> </div> </div> </div>Trading favors or building capital to use for trading favors can make up a lot of the daily activities of the Courts even without getting into local particulars like the entry requirements of a given Court or the cover story for a given freehold's constituency \u2014 between the necessary prep work and follow-up for fetches, Huntsmen, and stranger (or more familiar) things, there's a good number of fronts that any given changeling might want to shore up or be compensated for shoring up (or picking apart \u2014 intrigue cuts in all directions).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Assuming I go with the four season based courts, what would actually change when, for example, Summer gave way to Autumn? </div> </div> </div>Summer loses the Crown for its ruler and its attendant influence over the local Hedge while Autumn gains those same advantages, and the predominant mood and theme of the freehold shifts to suit the Court in power as Autumn begins to give priority to Autumn Things with the weight of institutional praxis behind it \u2014 the oath a Court represents includes the promise that its concepts will be evoked by its members and their actions and appearances, and a Crown brings with it the expectation that its bearer will rule.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Does the court that is currently in power get to issue rules to the freehold or enforce/encourage seasonal traditions? </div> </div> </div>Broadly speaking, yes. Current Monarchs tend to be supernaturally persuasive in a fashion that scales with how strongly they embody their Courts, and delegating to high-ranking lesser nobility in other Courts can get a good amount done.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Apart from the festivities associated with each court, would your 'average' changeling would they notice the change? </div> </div> </div>A Courtless changeling from outside the freehold might not spot the difference between the Summer Court in a freehold where they rule and a Summer Court where they don't (at least without taking a long look at the Hedge), but if the change is recent enough a respectable level of Empathy or Socialize or Politics might pick up on the difference.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T13:03:01-07:00","id":1072672,"title":"","content":"We'll have a fair bit about what they do and how they transition in the 2e core. For example:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chapter 1, by Ethan Skemp</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"> <b>High Summer:</b> Summer stands. When the Crimson Court is in power, it marshals the freehold\u2019s defense. A Summer monarch doesn\u2019t precisely <i>militarize</i> a freehold \u2014 though some would like to, or have tried. The Lost are individuals, and a freehold\u2019s populace is full of people who might man a barricade in a time of need, but have no interest in making discipline and chain of command the new normal. But the Iron Spear usually has to spend three seasons watching the other Courts ignore martial concerns. When they take power, it\u2019s time to clean the guns and sharpen the blades.<br /> <br /> Kings and Queens of Summer are exceptionally intimidating creatures. If you want to avoid conflict, you join some other Court where it\u2019s okay to hide or talk your way out of trouble. Crimson Courtiers test each other all the time, whether it\u2019s sparring to blow off steam, settling who\u2019s best with a sword or stick, or arguing over the best tactic for blasting out a warren of dangerous hobgoblins. The monarchs of Summer have had to prove themselves constantly, and it shows. A tower of steel-cable muscle and scars flexes a killing strength in each finger. An elegant diplomat with cold iron in his voice never asks for anything twice. A plainly dressed woman seems smaller than she is until her thumb brushes up against the hilt of her blade, and the smell of blood seems to surround her. A crooked man in sunset regalia proposes daring offensives backed by seemingly uncountable layers of strategy.<br /> <br /> An ascendant Summer monarch tends to focus on offense or defense. Defense involves activities such as gathering useful tokens of war, setting watchers on potential Hedge points of entry, building up the armory, and extracting pacts of alliance from whatever neighbors can be trusted to keep their word. Offense entails scouting missions deeper into the Hedge, grand hunts of particularly dangerous hobgoblins, and moving on tempting targets of opportunity. More fetches die when the Summer Court is in power than at any other time.<br /> <br /> <b>Low Summer:</b> When another season holds power, the Iron Spear insists on offering counsel. A Summer advisor stands as close to the throne as she can, fully armed. She defers to the reigning monarch in most things, like a good soldier, but <i>always</i> has an opinion when there\u2019s a mention of a Huntsman, or of the Gentry.<br /> <br /> High-ranking Summer Courtiers tend to split between looking inward and outward. Focusing inward is usually a matter of keeping the freehold defenses shored up. It\u2019s common practice to organize self-defense and physical training for interested parties, even weapons training for both ballistics and hand-to-hand combat.<br /> <br /> Looking outward entails many things, but small offensives against the Others in particular. A hunt during Low Summer might not be large and grandiose, but a few truly dedicated Summer soldiers can do some real damage. In most freeholds, a Courtier of Wrath keeps something like a bounty system running year-round, making public the descriptions, last known whereabouts, and names (if available) of the freehold\u2019s most dangerous known enemies. The payments for a Summer bounty are as strange and tempting as you might expect \u2014 cash is certainly possible, if gauche, but the truly dangerous targets are worth weapons and tokens and pledges.<br /> <br /> Lower-ranking Summer Courtiers find ways to serve the freehold. Obviously, they provide the lion\u2019s share of soldiers, sentinels, or constabulary. Standing guard isn\u2019t a full-time job \u2014 most freeholds aren\u2019t nearly large enough to support that \u2014 but the Iron Spear is there when needed. Some take well to crafting, be it gunsmithing, archaic weapons and armor, or restoring and improving vehicles.<br /> <br /> The Iron Spear encourages a volunteer culture in times of Low Summer, even outside the prospect of the hunt. Keeping busy is a good way to maintain or further your Court standing. In the absence of more organized activities, Crimson Courtiers focus their energy into action \u2014vigorous exercise, athletic competitions, martial training, Hedge raids, street races, poetry slams, all manner of pursuits. Wrath is a smoldering burden, and a responsible Summer courtier (they\u2019re not all responsible) needs to direct all that furious energy into something productive.<br /> <br /> To be Summer Court is to remember the necessity of vigilance, year-round. Most Crimson Courtiers understand joy, just not unfettered joy. They dance and sing and even laugh, sometimes, at the freehold\u2019s celebrations, but the Iron Spear is the designated driver. At least one of them\u2019s always sober, eyes on the exits.</div> </div> </div> </div>Note that non-seasonal Courts don't necessarily share power in the same way. For example, the French Market's Courts of Coin, Barter, Favors, and Shady Deals all function in their different specialties at the same time.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-03-2017, 04:06 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T16:27:59-07:00","id":1072759,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1072672#post1072672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll have a fair bit about what they do and how they transition in the 2e core. For example:<br /> <br /> Note that non-seasonal Courts don't necessarily share power in the same way. For example, the French Market's Courts of Coin, Barter, Favors, and Shady Deals all function in their different specialties at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div>Curse you Rose; I was already hyped for Changeling 2e, and now I want to play a game all the more! D:<br /> <br /> On a more serious note, this is a really interesting thing to learn, and it's making me factor it into my own long-worked on Changeling courts idea...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T17:52:14-07:00","id":1072817,"title":"","content":"That sounds cool.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-03T22:37:09-07:00","id":1072954,"title":"","content":"Thanks Satchel, your comments have got me thinking. <br /> <br /> Glad to hear the 2e is going into more detail on how the courts operate. I think the 1e dealt with the individuals and antagonist well, but wasn't quite clear enough on the day to day background. That might have just been been me, or it could be that after mainly playing VtM and VtR for so long and reading most of their novels, I've been spoilt with an abundance of background. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3955-roguewind","name":"Roguewind","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T01:27:42-07:00","id":1072991,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rose Bailey</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1072672#post1072672\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We'll have a fair bit about what they do and how they transition in the 2e core. For example:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Note that non-seasonal Courts don't necessarily share power in the same way. For example, the French Market's Courts of Coin, Barter, Favors, and Shady Deals all function in their different specialties at the same time.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> so excited for Changeling 2E! does this excerpt mean that CtL 2e will have sample courts (including the seasonal ones) in chapter 1?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T02:49:43-07:00","id":1073009,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1072991#post1072991\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">so excited for Changeling 2E! does this excerpt mean that CtL 2e will have sample courts (including the seasonal ones) in chapter 1?</div> </div> </div> </div>*Blinks*<br /> *Looks back at the quote*<br /> So.... I guess chapter 1's been severely reorganized.... Wonder if that means kiths aren't the x splat anymore, which would be disappointing.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/904596-geniuses-and-gramarie\" target=\"_blank\">Genius templates</a>: Super Science Mini-Template for Demon: the Descent<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1337874-oracle-the-endbringers-fan-splat\" target=\"_blank\">Oracle the Endbringers</a>: Time-Manipulator Fan-Splat","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/8331-milo-v3","name":"milo v3","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar8331_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1505"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T05:27:04-07:00","id":1073048,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>milo v3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073009#post1073009\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">*Blinks*<br /> *Looks back at the quote*<br /> So.... I guess chapter 1's been severely reorganized.... Wonder if that means kiths aren't the x splat anymore, which would be disappointing.</div> </div> </div> </div> I didn't notice that, Kith/Seemings we're chapter 1, I'm worried now that they got kid of the new Seeming Kith rules.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:31:24-07:00","id":1073078,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073048#post1073048\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I didn't notice that, Kith/Seemings we're chapter 1, I'm worried now that they got kid of the new Seeming Kith rules.</div> </div> </div> </div>It could be that Kith/Seemings &amp; a few sample courts are all in an expanded chapter 1.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:37:15-07:00","id":1073080,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert D</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073078#post1073078\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It could be that Kith/Seemings &amp; a few sample courts are all in an expanded chapter 1.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm going to go with this ^ here. In every Second Edition book I have, Chapter 1 is a mixture of X-Splats and Y-Splats. This is true in Vampire, Werewolf, Mage, Beast, and Promethean. I can't recall off the top of my head if this is strictly accurate to Demon, but the point stands. I imagine that Chapter 1 of Changeling 2E is going to be Kiths, Seemings, and the Seasonal Courts, which means it is going to be a really freaking huge chapter.<br /> <br /> The other sample Courts are probably going to be in the settings chapter that has sample Freeholds, since it's virtually impossible in Changeling 2E to have a setting <i>without </i>discussing the Courts.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/1127694-arcanist-s-homebrew-hub\" target=\"_blank\"><b>My Homebrew Hub</b></a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4152-arcanist","name":"Arcanist","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1232"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T06:44:15-07:00","id":1073086,"title":"","content":"I'm very glad Seasonal Courts are returning with background information in 2E corebook. That makes me <i>almost</i> convinced that 2E <b>Changeling</b> will be game for me. ( As I LOVE Courts of Seasons... )","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:03:22-07:00","id":1073094,"title":"","content":"And it looks like there will still be non-Seasonal Courts and Court creation options too based on Rose's previous comments. Something for everyone! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> (HUGE Seasonal Court fan myself, but and eager to see the non-Seasonal Courts too) <i>Originally posted by <b>Rose Bailey</b> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1072672#post1072672\">View Post</a></i><br /> <i>We'll have a fair bit about what they do and how they transition in the 2e core. For example:<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Note that non-seasonal Courts don't necessarily share power in the same way. For example, the French Market's Courts of Coin, Barter, Favors, and Shady Deals all function in their different specialties at the same time.</i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12074-robert-d","name":"Robert D","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"434"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T07:06:31-07:00","id":1073095,"title":"","content":"Courts will likely be in chapter 2; so far chapters 1 and 3 have been posted, with chapter 1 all but completed and chapter 3 in a close state.<br /> <br /> Edit: or sample courts will be in chapter 1 and court creation will be in chapter 2. Seems that there is some reorganization after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5803,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","user":"Taidragon","date":". 04-04-2017, 10:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5803-taidragon","name":"Taidragon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5803_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1038"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T09:37:13-07:00","id":1073188,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073086#post1073086\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm very glad Seasonal Courts are returning with background information in 2E corebook. That makes me <i>almost</i> convinced that 2E <b>Changeling</b> will be game for me. ( As I LOVE Courts of Seasons... )</div> </div> </div> </div>They were always going to be in there? David just hadn't shown them because y'all were familiar with them and wanted to show how the Freehold system could be used to do things other than that, particularly since prior to 2nd Edition there was literally no support for anyone trying to make a unique Freehold system on their own. But the Seasons were always transparently <i>there</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:09:06-07:00","id":1073223,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073188#post1073188\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">They were always going to be in there? David just hadn't shown them because y'all were familiar with them and wanted to show how the Freehold system could be used to do things other than that, particularly since prior to 2nd Edition there was literally no support for anyone trying to make a unique Freehold system on their own. But the Seasons were always transparently <i>there</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div> As someone who saw the David Hill version of the Autumn Court and now this one, how different are they in fluff and mechanics, I'm just curious as to what expect.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2241-omegaphallic","name":"Omegaphallic","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3435"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:30:35-07:00","id":1073235,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Omegaphallic</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1072653-freeholds?p=1073223#post1073223\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> As someone who saw the David Hill version of the Autumn Court and now this one, how different are they in fluff and mechanics, I'm just curious as to what expect.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, no doubt. My point to Hamster was more that the strange notion that Seasons was somehow missing was false.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-04-04T10:45:01-07:00","id":1073243,"title":"","content":"Quick info: Changeling follows the chapter structure of the other 2e books. In the final version, we have brought back full splat writeups for the Seasonal Courts in Chapter 1, rather than positioning them as shorter example Courts for Miami. Not all Court systems have the same supernatural structure or types of powers, but all of the core book Courts do have Mantles.<br /> <br /> (BTW, I might not be around much this week. I suffered a very painful back injury last night, and have to stay horizontal most of the time, and I don't yet know how fast I'll recover.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Cavaliers of Mars Creator</b><br /> <b>Retired CofD Lead</b><br /> <br /> Check out my <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Rose%20Bailey\" target=\"_blank\">guides to </a><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/261142/BITE-ME-How-to-Write-Vampire?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire</a> and my <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/browse/pub/4895/Fantasy-Heartbreaker?affiliate_id=453494&amp;src=OPPf\" target=\"_blank\">indie games</a>!","edited":{"userid":2,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","user":"Rose Bailey","date":". 04-04-2017, 01:48 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2-rose-bailey","name":"Rose Bailey","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2361"}]},"thankedby":[]},{